WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.960
Red build. Real bug, or flaky test?

00:00:04.017 --> 00:00:08.027
At Google, almost 16% of tests show some
flakiness.

00:00:09.684 --> 00:00:16.006
And every team rebuilds the same plumbing:
waits, drivers, screenshots and reports,

00:00:16.006 --> 00:00:19.814
once for web, again for mobile, and again
for API.

00:00:21.051 --> 00:00:25.820
SHAFT is one open-source Java engine for
web, mobile, API,

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:28.451
database and command-line tests.

00:00:29.718 --> 00:00:34.249
It is built on the standards your team
already trusts: Selenium,

00:00:34.249 --> 00:00:35.948
Appium and REST Assured.

00:00:36.985 --> 00:00:41.335
Waiting is built in, so your tests stop
guessing when a page is ready.

00:00:42.385 --> 00:00:45.664
Every run produces an Allure report with
steps and

00:00:45.664 --> 00:00:48.615
screenshots that anyone on the team can
read.

00:00:49.852 --> 00:00:53.592
And the same tests move from a laptop to a
Selenium

00:00:53.592 --> 00:00:56.892
Grid or BrowserStack by changing one
setting.

00:00:57.952 --> 00:01:03.053
Adopting it is low risk. The upgrade tool
compiles your project first,

00:01:03.053 --> 00:01:08.082
keeps your existing tests, and restores
every file if anything fails.

00:01:09.519 --> 00:01:15.429
AI help is optional. Capture, Doctor and
Heal work without any AI provider.

00:01:16.486 --> 00:01:21.884
SHAFT is MIT licensed and built in public
since 2018,

00:01:21.884 --> 00:01:25.856
with 216 releases from 62 contributors.

00:01:27.319 --> 00:01:34.269
Generate a ready-to-run project in about
90 seconds at shafthq.github.io.

00:01:34.569 --> 00:01:37.899
Then pilot the upgrade on one repository
this sprint.

